    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d128-a4">

                <pb facs="0290" n="194" xml:id="pg194"/>

                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of Foreign Relations of Guatemala</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1874-04-16"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 16, 1874</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have this day addressed the licentiate
                    Don Vicente Dardon, minister plenipotentiary and envoy extraordinary of this
                    republic in North America, sending him a copy of the esteemed note of your
                    department, dated the 23d ultimo, and instructing him to do all in his power in
                    favor of the Nicaragua canal, in conjunction with the representative of your
                    country.</p>
                <p>In having the honor to state this to your excellency for the information of the
                    Chief Magistrate of your republic, I am happy to subscribe myself,</p>
                <p>Your obedient and faithful servant,</p>
                <closer><signed>MARCO A. SOTO.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>The <hi rendition="#italic">Minister of Foreign Relations of
                        Nicaragua.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
